hing you can do that i like a lot  of the objects and stuff that they have  in this game they have infected knives  that when you throw them at actual  people they will turn into infected and  that's really unique because what you  can do is if you don't want a lot of  conflict at a certain situation because  there's a lot of people there you can  throw one of these infected knives or an  infected arrow it would turn them and  they'll actually turn on the other  people there and you can use that to  take out bigger targets that are a lot  more hard for you as a character to take  them down and i think that's interesting  not to mention there's actually more  infected there's a lot more emphasis on  running at night i feel like the night  gameplay on this is a lot better than it  was in dying light one but i do feel  like it needed to be more intense than  it was in this game and what i mean by  that is i want dying lights night  gameplay because that's supposed to be  the most dangerous time to play dying  light and i feel like that's what  separates it from other zombie type like  games and i don't think that they go too  i don't think they go as far i'm going  to be real with you guys i feel like  what they need to do is it needs to be  one of those things where it doesn't  matter if you're on the rooftops it  doesn't matter if you're running through  the streets these zombies will come  after you now they do have incidences  where if you come across certain key  point zombies they will initiate what  called a chase and it's pretty much just  someone one of the zombies screaming and  it's alerting the rest of the zombies  that you're there but the thing is is i  never one time in this game felt like i  was in danger at night sure i would die  occasionally on this game and i died a  lot in terms of judging a fall and not  judging it correctly and i would die  from fall damage i never really died too  many times on actual zombies and i feel  like considering this is a zombie game  i'm tired of these companies not putting  enough fear on the zombies it kind of  feels like that point in the walking  dead where zombies is like a real key  point at the beginning of the series but  then when you get closer to the end of  the series or later on in the show it  turns out that zombies isn't the main  problem it's humans and i feel like  you're going to embrace that the  majority of the time in a zombie  apocalypse thing but i felt like you  could do both you don't have to do just  one you can make the zombies aggressive  you can make the zombies more effective  and more scary and you can also make the  humans be the divining pathetic  creatures that they are at some points  of the game you could easily do both and  i and i always felt like especially in  dying light 2 when you get more of these  abilities the zombies aren't even an  issue anymore you could run from the  majority of them and i want that to  change i felt like you know when a  zombie grabs you it should be a rat but  it's not like that it's you know for the  most part you can have abilities where  you can jump on the zombies to get more  of the air you can get on the rooftops  relatively easy now there are zombies on  the rooftops but there's not a lot so as  long as you stick on the roofs you'll be  fine they're for the most part are never  gonna get to you up there now if you  initiate a chase and you run on the  rooftops they will most definitely chase  you anywhere you go but to be honest  with you guys even the chases are not  that bad because when you do outpost you  get these uv lights that's on the actual  outpost and for the most part if you run  into a chase or you initiate a chase  it's literally just you either bringing  up the map and finding the next outpost  it's nearest to you which sometimes can  be a bother especially if you're on the  ground and you activate one of these  because that means a lot of the times  you're going to be climbing a lot of  stu